        <mxCell id="gul241T2A2ipK3npSPCq-89" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=top;rounded=0;fontColor=#FFFFFF;fontSize=10;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;opacity=90;opacityGroup=1;" value="IKEv2/IPsec VPN Tunnel (logical, no cable)" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="18" width="400" x="1460" y="220" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="gul241T2A2ipK3npSPCq-90" edge="1" parent="1" style="rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;defaultLabelBackgroundColor=page;labelPadding=0 4;startArrow=none;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#FF5C5C;strokeWidth=2;dashed=1;dashPattern=8 4;fontColor=#FFFFFF;fontSize=9;labelBackgroundColor=#1E1E1E;opacity=90;opacityGroup=1;" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint x="1575" y="242" as="sourcePoint" />
            <mxPoint x="1745" y="242" as="targetPoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="gul241T2A2ipK3npSPCq-91" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=top;rounded=0;fontColor=#FFFFFF;fontSize=10;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;opacity=90;opacityGroup=1;" value="Blocked by ACL (R3)" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="18" width="400" x="1460" y="258" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="gul241T2A2ipK3npSPCq-92" edge="1" parent="1" style="rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;defaultLabelBackgroundColor=page;labelPadding=0 4;strokeColor=#FF5C5C;strokeWidth=3;endArrow=cross;startArrow=cross;endSize=9;startSize=9;fontColor=#FFFFFF;fontSize=9;labelBackgroundColor=#1E1E1E;opacity=90;opacityGroup=1;" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint x="1575" y="280" as="sourcePoint" />
            <mxPoint x="1745" y="280" as="targetPoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="gul241T2A2ipK3npSPCq-93" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=top;rounded=0;fontColor=#FFFFFF;fontSize=9;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;opacity=90;opacityGroup=1;" value="Red box = assignment requirement (R1 to R4).  (n) = numbered reference in the paper.  Transit links 10.0.0.0/16 (/30s); internal 10.10.0.0/16; management VLAN 99 10.10.99.0/24 carries device management only." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="56" width="400" x="1460" y="312" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="gul241T2A2ipK3npSPCq-94" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#FF5C5C;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#FFFFFF;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;opacity=90;opacityGroup=1;" value="&lt;b&gt;R2  All VPN connections terminate at the VPN Server (12)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Edge firewall forwards IKE UDP 500/4500 and ESP only to&lt;br&gt;203.0.113.5 &amp;gt; 172.16.10.30. VPN is disabled on the edge&lt;br&gt;router, edge firewall, and internal firewall; any other VPN&lt;br&gt;attempt is dropped and logged (2)." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="76" width="420" x="1450" y="400" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="gul241T2A2ipK3npSPCq-95" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#FF5C5C;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#FFFFFF;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;opacity=90;opacityGroup=1;" value="&lt;b&gt;R1  VPN (laptop) reaches IT desktops, IT employees only (11)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;NPS network policy: Windows Group = IT-VPN-Users; all&lt;br&gt;other users rejected (22). NPS returns Class = it-vpn and&lt;br&gt;strongSwan assigns the IT pool 10.20.10.0/24 (13).&lt;br&gt;Internal FW: 10.20.10.0/24 &amp;gt; 10.10.30.0/24 TCP 3389 ALLOW;&lt;br&gt;10.20.10.0/24 &amp;gt; any other subnet DENY." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="89" width="420" x="1450" y="535" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="gul241T2A2ipK3npSPCq-96" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#FF5C5C;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#FFFFFF;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;opacity=90;opacityGroup=1;" value="&lt;b&gt;R3  Engineering and Finance/Accounting cannot communicate&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Separate VLANs 40 and 50 route only through the&lt;br&gt;distribution router (3). Inbound ACLs (20):&lt;br&gt;Vlan40: deny ip 10.10.40.0 0.0.0.255 10.10.50.0 0.0.0.255&lt;br&gt;Vlan50: deny ip 10.10.50.0 0.0.0.255 10.10.40.0 0.0.0.255&lt;br&gt;then permit ip any any." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="89" width="420" x="1450" y="905" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="gul241T2A2ipK3npSPCq-97" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#FF5C5C;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#FFFFFF;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;opacity=90;opacityGroup=1;" value="&lt;b&gt;R4  Daily vulnerability scans of every desktop&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Nessus &amp;quot;Daily Desktop Scan&amp;quot;: Frequency Daily, 01:00 (26).&lt;br&gt;Targets 10.10.30.0/24, 10.10.40.0/24, 10.10.50.0/24,&lt;br&gt;credentialed with a domain scan account (28).&lt;br&gt;Wake-on-LAN wakes powered-off desktops first (27).&lt;br&gt;Second pass at 12:00 rescans missed hosts, so every&lt;br&gt;desktop is scanned at least once per day." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="102" width="420" x="1450" y="1060" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="gul241T2A2ipK3npSPCq-98" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#FF5C5C;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#FFFFFF;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;opacity=90;opacityGroup=1;" value="&lt;b&gt;Required devices: 15 of 15 included&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Edge router, edge firewall, internal firewall, IDS, web proxy,&lt;br&gt;core router, distribution router, switches, web, FTP, VPN,&lt;br&gt;authentication, and antivirus servers, antivirus clients&lt;br&gt;(Defender on every desktop), vulnerability scanner." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="76" width="420" x="1450" y="1265" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="gul241T2A2ipK3npSPCq-99" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#FFFFFF;opacity=90;opacityGroup=1;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="348.4" width="1830" x="40" y="1610" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="gul241T2A2ipK3npSPCq-100" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;rounded=0;fontColor=#FFFFFF;fontSize=9;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;opacity=90;opacityGroup=1;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;&quot;&gt;REFERENCES (numbers match the reference list in the paper)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. JGraph Ltd., &quot;draw.io: Security first diagramming for teams.&quot; [Online]. Available: https://drawio.com/&lt;br&gt;2. K. Scarfone and P. Hoffman, &quot;Guidelines on Firewalls and Firewall Policy,&quot; NIST Special Publication 800-41 Rev. 1, National Institute of Standards and Technology, 2009. [Online]. Available: https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/sp/800/41/r1/final&lt;br&gt;3. Cisco Systems, &quot;Campus Network for High Availability Design Guide,&quot; Cisco Validated Design, 2008. [Online]. Available: https://www.cisco.com/en/US/docs/solutions/Enterprise/Campus/HA_campus_DG/hacampusdg.html&lt;br&gt;4. Cisco Systems, &quot;Cisco Catalyst 8300 Series Edge Platforms Data Sheet,&quot; 2026. [Online]. Available: https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/collateral/routers/catalyst-8300-series-edge-platforms/datasheet-c78-744088.html&lt;br&gt;6. Palo Alto Networks, &quot;PA-1400 Series Datasheet.&quot; [Online]. Available: https://www.paloaltonetworks.com/resources/datasheets/pa-1400-series&lt;br&gt;7. Cisco Systems, &quot;Cisco Catalyst 9200 Series Switches Data Sheet,&quot; 2026. [Online]. Available: https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/collateral/switches/catalyst-9200-series-switches/nb-06-cat9200-ser-data-sheet-cte-en.html&lt;br&gt;8. M. Tracy, W. Jansen, K. Scarfone, and T. Winograd, &quot;Guidelines on Securing Public Web Servers,&quot; NIST Special Publication 800-44 Version 2, National Institute of Standards and Technology, 2007. [Online]. Available: https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/sp/800/44/ver2/final&lt;br&gt;10. OpenBSD Project, &quot;sshd_config(5): OpenSSH daemon configuration file,&quot; OpenBSD manual pages. [Online]. Available: https://man.openbsd.org/sshd_config&lt;br&gt;11. M. Souppaya and K. Scarfone, &quot;Guide to Enterprise Telework, Remote Access, and Bring Your Own Device (BYOD) Security,&quot; NIST Special Publication 800-46 Rev. 2, National Institute of Standards and Technology, 2016. [Online]. Available: https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/sp/800/46/r2/final&lt;br&gt;12. E. Barker, Q. Dang, S. Frankel, K. Scarfone, and P. Wouters, &quot;Guide to IPsec VPNs,&quot; NIST Special Publication 800-77 Rev. 1, National Institute of Standards and Technology, 2020. [Online]. Available: https://doi.org/10.6028/NIST.SP.800-77r1&lt;br&gt;13. strongSwan Project, &quot;eap-radius Plugin,&quot; strongSwan documentation. [Online]. Available: https://docs.strongswan.org/docs/5.9/plugins/eap-radius.html&lt;br&gt;14. Fortinet, &quot;Technical Tip: FortiGate specifications using Enterprise Mix,&quot; Fortinet Community. [Online]. Available: https://community.fortinet.com/fortigate-3/technical-tip-fortigate-specifications-using-enterprise-mix-97095&lt;br&gt;15. Security Onion Solutions, &quot;Architecture,&quot; Security Onion 3 documentation. [Online]. Available: https://docs.securityonion.net/en/3/main/architecture&lt;br&gt;16. K. Scarfone and P. Mell, &quot;Guide to Intrusion Detection and Prevention Systems (IDPS),&quot; NIST Special Publication 800-94, National Institute of Standards and Technology, 2007. [Online]. Available: https://csrc.nist.gov/publications/detail/sp/800-94/final&lt;br&gt;17. Squid Project, &quot;Feature: SslBump Peek and Splice,&quot; Squid wiki. [Online]. Available: https://wiki.squid-cache.org/Features/SslPeekAndSplice&lt;br&gt;18. Cisco Systems, &quot;Cisco Catalyst 8500 Series Edge Platforms Data Sheet.&quot; [Online]. Available: https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/collateral/routers/catalyst-8500-series-edge-platforms/datasheet-c78-744089.html&lt;br&gt;19. Cisco Systems, &quot;Cisco Catalyst 9500 Se